ings.","period_end":"2024-12-31"},{"type":"redefinition","origin":"ai","summary":"The Term Loan maturity changed from 2027 to 2032 in the 2025 third-quarter filing.","period_end":"2025-09-30"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report substantial recurring purchases, sales, receivables, and payables with affiliates of Platinum Equity Advisors.","period_end":"2022-12-31"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"The Tax Receivable Agreement created a large related-party payment obligation to VPE Holdings and was later replaced with a fixed $100.0 million cash obligation.","period_end":"2022-12-31"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The March 2021 filing reports a post-period offering of $850.0 million of Senior Secured Notes due 2028.","period_end":"2021-09-30"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2022 filing reports that the Energy Labs dispute was settled for $21.5 million after earlier filings described a possible $34.5 million earn-out claim.","period_end":"2021-12-31"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2020/A filing reports materially different 2019 net income, tax expense, and operating cash flow than the FY2019 filing.","period_end":"2019-12-31"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2020/A filing reports materially different 2019 nine-month and third-quarter results than the earlier filing.","period_end":"2019-09-30"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2020/A filing revises 2020 quarterly and full-year net income and diluted share data.","period_end":"2020-12-31"}],"narratives":[{"period_end":"2025-09-30","narrative":"The filing reports deferred revenue expected over later periods, debt maturities, and bank guarantees and bonds requiring customer payments for non-performance. It also records the Great Lakes acquisition and continued capital-expenditure and lease commitments."},{"period_end":"2025-12-31","narrative":"The quarter disclosed backlog subject to cancellation or rescheduling, deferred revenue, debt and lease maturities, and contingent acquisition consideration. It also reports bank guarantees and bonds requiring customer payments for non-performance and significant research and development spending."},{"period_end":"2026-03-31","narrative":"The filing reports noncurrent deferred revenue, contingent acquisition consideration, substantial long-dated debt, and bank guarantees and bonds. Lease and capital-expenditure plans were also disclosed for the year."},{"period_end":"2026-06-30","narrative":"The quarter disclosed contingent earnouts, later-period deferred revenue, long-dated debt, bank guarantees and bonds, and substantial lease and capital-expenditure plans. The filing also reports a committed revolving credit facility and conditional expansion capacity."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue reached $11.5 billion over the trailing year, while expenses were $9.2 billion. Revenue grew 19% per year against 16% expense growth, with committed obligations declining 3% per year.","debt":"Leases add $82 million to the $2.9 billion reported debt balance, bringing total committed money to $3.0 billion. That is 1.0x reported debt, so leases add little to the headline obligation.","wall":"The main pressure sits in the next five years: $5.7 billion of debt and lease payments are due against $27 million of future revenue promised for that period. The filing also shows $82 million due after year five, without matching future revenue in that band.","flags_note":"The sharpest flags concern affiliate ties and obligations outside ordinary debt. Filings report sales, purchases, receivables, and payables with Platinum Equity affiliates, plus bank guarantees and bonds tied to customer payments for non-performance. They also show five of 28 quarters changed by reconciliation, alongside revised results and changing maturity disclosures."}}